Key details:
- Line endings: files may or may not end with a newline. When reading, split lines while preserving the newline. Use `read()` and split. The last line of paradise-lost.txt has no trailing newline, but the expected output appends "\n" to each line. So the simplest approach: read the whole content, split with `splitlines(keepends=True)`... but the last line of paradise-lost has no newline, and the expected output has a newline. So we should normalize: strip trailing newlines from each line and add "\n" to each output line.

